+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive, framework-free coffee homepage with a My Account dashboard.
+
+## Account features
+
+- Register a local customer profile with a native WebAuthn passkey.
+- Sign in using a device fingerprint, face, PIN, or compatible security key.
+- Add, rename, and remove saved passkeys. Removing the final key is blocked until a backup is added.
+- Update the name and email after a fresh passkey assertion.
+- Reauthenticate explicitly or before adding or changing passkeys.
+- Sign out; reloading the page also ends the in-memory session.
+- Browser cancellation, unsupported environments, duplicate registrations, and verification failures show recoverable errors.
+
+## Scope
+
+This repository is a static site with no authentication server. The UI explicitly identifies the implementation as a browser-local preview. Profiles and credential public keys are stored in localStorage, while private keys stay with the authenticator. Actual native WebAuthn ceremonies and local Web Crypto signature verification are implemented; no successful authentication is simulated.
+
+**This is not a production security boundary.** Browser-local data and JavaScript can be changed by the browser user. Accounts are available only in the browser where registered. Clearing site data removes the profile and registered public keys, although the authenticator may still retain its passkeys. There is no recovery, email ownership verification, cross-device account synchronization, order service, or rewards backend. Changes to email do not rewrite the account label already saved in a password manager.
+
+For production, replace local account persistence and verification with a trusted authentication service that issues single-use expiring challenges, validates registrations and assertions on the server, enforces authorization, persists credentials and profiles, and manages secure sessions and account recovery. Serve over HTTPS; localhost is also supported by WebAuthn during development.
+
+## Validation
+
+`npm test` runs Node's built-in test runner. Tests generate real ECDSA signatures and exercise verification, origin and RP checks, user verification, replay counters, unsupported browsers, and safe HTML rendering. `node --check app.js` checks syntax. No dependencies or build step are needed. Native device prompts are not exercised by these tests.
+
+## References
+
+- [Web Authentication API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Authentication_API)
+- [Authenticator data](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Authentication_API/Authenticator_data)
+- [Passkey public key extraction](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AuthenticatorAttestationResponse/getPublicKey)
+
+Photography is loaded from Unsplash. Typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts; local sans-serif fallbacks are provided.
